---
type Section={id:string;title:string;body:string[];example?:string;points?:string[];source?:[string,string]};
type DeepGuide={intro:string;sections:Section[];questions:[string,string][]};
const data:Record<string,DeepGuide>={
 'hijama-date-planner':{
 intro:'A lunar-date reference and an evidence-aware guide to Hijama. Calendars, hadith authenticity and clinical effectiveness are three different questions.',
 sections:[
 {id:'hijama-types',title:'Wet and dry cupping are different procedures',body:['Dry cupping places a cup on intact skin to produce suction. Wet cupping involves breaking the skin before or during suction, exposing the person to additional bleeding and infection risks. The two approaches should not be treated as interchangeable when assessing evidence.','Cupping is practised in different cultures and sometimes called Hijama in Islamic contexts. The date planner does not choose a treatment, location on the body, practitioner or indication.'],points:['Dry cupping: suction without skin puncture','Wet cupping: involves skin puncture and blood exposure','Neither replaces established medical investigation or treatment'],source:['NCCIH cupping overview','https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/cupping']},
 {id:'hijama-report',title:'What is actually reported about 17, 19 and 21?',body:['Sunan Abi Dawud 3861 reports a connection between cupping and the 17th, 19th and 21st of a lunar month. Sunnah.com lists an assessment of Hasan from al-Albani for that report. Assessments of related date and weekday narrations differ, so this planner deliberately avoids presenting one universal ruling.','A report in a hadith compilation is not equivalent to a modern clinical trial. A phrase about healing in a narration cannot establish that an invasive procedure cures all diseases.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 3861 with grading','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:3861']},
 {id:'hijama-calculation',title:'How the Hijri conversion works',body:['The calculator uses the Umm al-Qura calendar as an estimate, mapping each 17th, 19th and 21st Hijri day onto its corresponding Gregorian date. Select 3, 6 or 12 months ahead; a one-day adjustment shows a nearby possibility rather than verified local moon-sighting data.','Remember that an Islamic date begins at local sunset, whereas exported calendar reminders are all-day Gregorian events. A calendar export cannot identify the start of a lunar day at your location.'],example:'If 17 Safar is calculated as 28 August, a local moon-sighting difference could place the equivalent civil date on 27 or 29 August. Neither alternative can be verified just by pressing the adjustment control.'},
 {id:'hijama-evidence',title:'What research can and cannot establish',body:['NCCIH reports that many studies are low quality. There is limited evidence of possible benefit for pain, with insufficient high-quality research for other conditions. Cupping should not be advertised as effective for infertility, chronic infections, hypertension, detoxification or any particular disease without reliable condition-specific evidence.','Temporary marks and skin irritation are common considerations. Other harms include infection, burns or scars, and bloodborne infections from inadequately sterilised equipment.'],source:['NCCIH – research quality and safety','https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/cupping']},
 {id:'hijama-practitioner',title:'Practical safety questions before booking',body:['Ask the practitioner to explain their training, infection-control procedures, single-use sterile equipment, handling of blood and sharps, aftercare and what symptoms warrant medical help.','Tell a clinician about medicines that affect bleeding, a history of fainting, anaemia, clotting disorders, pregnancy or skin conditions before invasive cupping. A professional should also discuss whether any planned procedure is appropriate at all.'],points:['Are sterile single-use instruments used?','What qualifications and infection-control protocols apply?','What adverse effects and aftercare should I know about?','Should I consult my GP or treating clinician first?']},
 {id:'hijama-faq',title:'Do I have to wait for a particular date?',body:['The tool does not determine a religious obligation or medical need to wait until 17, 19 or 21. If you are seeking medical evaluation for pain, swelling, severe symptoms or another condition, do not delay appropriate care while waiting for a lunar date.','The safest use of this planner is learning which dates a cited narration references, not deciding whether or when you should undergo an invasive intervention.']}
 ],
 questions:[['Is Hijama automatically safe because it is traditional?','No. Wet cupping breaks the skin and introduces specific safety risks. Traditional use is not proof of safety for every person.'],['Are Mondays or other weekdays forbidden?','Reports about particular weekdays have varying assessments. This website does not declare a weekday prohibited.'],['Can Hijama replace migraine medication or an assessment for swelling?','No. Seek clinical advice for persistent or concerning symptoms and do not suspend prescribed treatment because of the calendar.']]
 },
 'duha-prayer-time':{
 intro:'A practical guide to calculating a voluntary morning prayer window while distinguishing astronomical events from estimates and scholarly conventions.',
 sections:[
 {id:'duha-definition',title:'What are Duha and Ishraq?',body:['Duha is a voluntary prayer after the sunrise prohibition has passed and before the sun reaches its zenith. Ishraq commonly refers to prayer near the beginning of that period, though terminology and practice vary.','The calculator begins with actual sunrise and Dhuhr start estimates, not Fajr or the moment the sun first appears above the horizon.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 720 – Two rakahs of Duha','https://sunnah.com/muslim:720']},
 {id:'duha-margins',title:'Why are there 20-minute and 10-minute margins?',body:['The tool uses 20 minutes after sunrise and 10 minutes before Dhuhr as cautious default planning offsets. These are not universal legal cutoffs. The time for the sun to rise above the prohibited period depends on season and location; discuss locally observed practice with a knowledgeable scholar.','If your mosque publishes times, activate manual entry to use its sunrise and Dhuhr schedule. You can change the optional buffer settings, but a shorter buffer is not a ruling that the prayer becomes valid at that exact minute.'],example:'Sunrise 07:00, Dhuhr 12:30, start buffer 20 minutes and end buffer 10 minutes produces a suggested 07:20–12:20 window.'},
 {id:'duha-when-best',title:'When is Duha especially recommended?',body:['Sahih Muslim 748a describes the prayer of the penitent at a later morning period when the sun has become warm. This indicates a merit associated with later Duha, rather than restricting the whole prayer to one fixed clock time.','For practical planning, choose a time comfortably between the early sunrise prohibition and the approach of Dhuhr.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 748a – Later-morning Duha','https://sunnah.com/muslim:748a']},
 {id:'duha-rakats',title:'How many rakahs?',body:['Two rakahs are well-attested. Reports and juristic guidance also discuss four, six and eight rakahs. If you pray additional units, do so in a way consistent with the guidance you follow.','No browser calculation can decide the acceptance of a prayer. The timing result is an aid to planning, not a religious certificate.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 720 – Encouragement to pray Duha','https://sunnah.com/muslim:720']},
 {id:'duha-method',title:'Calculated city times versus mosque times',body:['The example-city selector uses coordinates, the Muslim World League calculation preset and the city time zone. Sunrise and Dhuhr do not depend on every setting that affects Fajr and Isha, but local timetables can still differ because of rounding, elevation, conventions and corrections.','Cities are examples, not proof of the user’s current location. Where high-latitude or unusual conditions make results unreliable, use authoritative local guidance.'],points:['Choose your city and intended date','Compare sunrise/Dhuhr against your mosque','Apply margins with an understanding of their approximate nature','Check local practice for the disliked interval around zenith']},
 {id:'duha-questions',title:'Common timing misunderstandings',body:['Duha is not Fajr, and it is not prayed the instant sunrise occurs. Dhuhr starts after the sun passes the meridian, so an estimated Dhuhr start is only a useful proxy for approaching the zenith.','A future-date estimate is not an automatically updated live mosque timetable. Check daylight-saving adjustments and the date you have selected.']}
 ],
 questions:[['Can I pray right at sunrise?','Do not use the exact sunrise time as the beginning of Duha. Wait until the prohibited sunrise interval has passed.'],['Is the later part of the window mandatory?','No. There is a reported virtue in later-morning Duha, while the prayer has a wider allowable window.'],['Are the margins guaranteed worldwide?','No. They are adjustable planning choices, not universally agreed legal cutoffs.']]
 },
 'istikhara-guide':{
 intro:'The authentic Istikhara method is prayer, supplication and thoughtful action—without requiring dreams or extraordinary signs.',
 sections:[
 {id:'istikhara-when',title:'When should you perform Istikhara?',body:['Istikhara is taught for matters where you are considering a permissible choice: for example, a suitable job, moving house or deciding between reasonable options. It is not a substitute for an obligation, a reason to pursue something prohibited or a replacement for advice on a dangerous situation.','Gather relevant facts, consult appropriately and ask Allah for guidance. The supplication asks that good be facilitated and harmful choices turned away.'],source:['Sahih al-Bukhari 1166 – Teaching of Istikhara','https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1166']},
 {id:'istikhara-steps',title:'Step-by-step method',body:['First perform the necessary purification. Pray two non-obligatory rakahs at a permissible time, then recite the reported dua and mention your specific matter. The precise position of the supplication relative to salam is discussed by scholars; follow credible local teaching.','There is no requirement to recite a specially assigned surah in each rakah. The reported dua is reproduced in Arabic in the interactive guide above.'],points:['Identify a permissible choice and gather facts','Make wudu as required and pray two voluntary rakahs','Recite the Istikhara dua with the matter in mind','Consult, decide and act responsibly; continue to make dua']},
 {id:'istikhara-dua',title:'Understanding the supplication',body:['The words affirm that Allah knows what a person does not, has power over what a person cannot control, and can open or close a path according to what is truly good. The closing request is for the best outcome and contentment with it.','Arabic pronunciation and wording matter; the on-page Latin transliteration is approximate. For accuracy, learn the Arabic from a qualified teacher or trustworthy recorded recitation.'],source:['Arabic and English text – Bukhari 1166','https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1166']},
 {id:'istikhara-no-dream',title:'Do you need a dream, colour or feeling?',body:['The hadith itself teaches the two-rakah prayer and the dua; it does not say that a person must dream, see a colour or wait for a mystical sign. You should not insist that all obstacles or comforts are proof of one particular divine verdict.','After thoughtful effort, choose the most reasonable lawful course and trust in Allah while taking normal precautions.']},
 {id:'istikhara-repeat',title:'Repeating Istikhara and seeking counsel',body:['If the matter remains uncertain, you may continue making dua and seek further advice. The authenticity of particular fixed numbers of repetitions should be checked rather than invented.','Other people can offer good counsel, but a decision affecting your legal or medical wellbeing may require professional information as well as spiritual reflection.']},
 {id:'istikhara-example',title:'Worked example: deciding between two jobs',body:['You have two lawful job offers. Compare responsibilities, hours, pay, family impact and work conditions. Seek advice from people who understand your circumstances. Pray two rakahs and ask Allah to ease what is good.','If you later choose one role, this is not a claim that the site has predicted the unseen. It illustrates using prayer alongside responsible decision-making.'],example:'Decision: “Should I accept job A?” Facts: travel time, family commitments, suitability and contract terms. Action: Istikhara plus informed consultation, followed by a practical decision.'}
 ],
 questions:[['Is Istikhara only for marriage?','No. It may be used for many permissible decisions.'],['Do I need to see a dream?','No. Dreams are not required by the authentic report.'],['Can I read the Arabic from the screen?','Yes, as an aid. Use reliable teaching for correct recitation, and consult qualified guidance for circumstances affecting prayer.']]
 },
 'friday-sunnah-checklist':{
 intro:'Understand the evidence and practical purpose behind Friday preparation without treating a checklist as a substitute for religious guidance.',
 sections:[
 {id:'friday-essential',title:'Jumuah, obligation and exemptions',body:['The Friday congregational prayer is an obligation for those to whom it applies, subject to recognised exemptions and individual circumstances. The checkbox list intentionally does not declare whether someone is required to attend.','Consult a qualified scholar about illness, travel, family circumstances or accessibility rather than using a generic web checklist to decide.'],source:['Quran 62:9 – Friday congregation','https://quran.com/62/9']},
 {id:'friday-ghusl',title:'Ghusl, cleanliness and fragrance',body:['Authentic reports strongly emphasise Friday washing, but schools differ in how they classify its legal status. Clean clothing and avoiding unpleasant odours show consideration for others at the congregation.','The checklist is a reminder to prepare; it does not decide whether someone may pray with an injury or needs an alternative purification ruling.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 846a – Friday ghusl','https://sunnah.com/muslim:846a']},
 {id:'friday-attend',title:'Arriving and listening to the khutbah',body:['Arriving in good time helps avoid disruption. Attentively listening to the sermon is an important part of the congregation; avoid chatting or distracting others.','Follow the local mosque’s actual Jumuah start and khutbah times. Some mosques offer multiple sessions, especially in places with limited capacity.'],source:['Sahih al-Bukhari 881 – Early arrival','https://sunnah.com/bukhari:881']},
 {id:'friday-kahf',title:'Surah Al-Kahf and its reported Friday virtue',body:['Surah Al-Kahf is chapter 18 of the Quran. Reports about its particular virtue on Fridays have been graded differently; keep the distinction between reciting Quran generally and making an unqualified assertion about every report.','For reading convenience, the checklist links directly to Quran.com/18. The browser does not claim to verify that your recitation was complete.'],source:['Read Surah Al-Kahf','https://quran.com/18']},
 {id:'friday-salawat',title:'Salawat and dua',body:['Sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ is encouraged in Islamic sources, including reports specifically discussing Friday. Many narrations also mention an opportunity for accepted supplication on Friday, with scholarly discussions about its timing.','A practical habit is to reserve an unhurried period for remembrance and personal dua without turning a proposed schedule into an obligation.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 1047 – Friday salawat','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:1047']},
 {id:'friday-tracker',title:'How to use this private weekly checklist',body:['The browser stores only a list of checked items for the selected Friday. No account, public profile or worship score is created. The entries stay on the device and can be reset or lost when browser storage is cleared.','The aim is practical planning: get ready, attend appropriately if obligated and able, and maintain worship with sincerity.'],example:'On Thursday night, check when your mosque holds Jumuah. On Friday, set aside time for appropriate preparation, travel and worship without rushing.'}
 ],
 questions:[['Is each listed action fard?','No. This checklist combines acts with different juridical classifications.'],['Can I tick items after Friday?','The checklist records your choices locally; it does not measure religious merit.'],['Does my local mosque time appear automatically?','No. Check your mosque directly for iqamah and khutbah details.']]
 },
 'islamic-will-planner':{
 intro:'A UK-focused preparation guide separating Islamic inheritance questions from the national legal formalities needed for an enforceable will.',
 sections:[
 {id:'will-two-layers',title:'Two distinct layers: religious distribution and civil law',body:['Islamic inheritance rules concern debts, bequests and prescribed heirs. A will must also satisfy the law of the place where it takes effect. A handwritten wish list or unexecuted computer download should not be represented as legally binding.','The worksheet intentionally does not compute shares, invent an executor, offer model legal clauses or ask for bank account numbers.'],source:['GOV.UK – Making a will','https://www.gov.uk/make-will']},
 {id:'will-heirs',title:'Islamic heirs and the estate',body:['Quran 4:11–12 and 4:176 discuss specified inheritance portions. A precise distribution depends on who survives the deceased, their relationships and other legal and juristic factors. Assets, valid debts and any permissible bequests may also affect the available estate.','A simplified percentage calculator can mislead when family relationships, surviving spouses, parents or other heirs are missing. Have the complete circumstances reviewed by a qualified Islamic inheritance specialist.'],source:['Quran 4:11 – Heir shares','https://quran.com/4/11']},
 {id:'will-bequests',title:'Wills, charitable wishes and the one-third discussion',body:['Classical jurisprudence distinguishes prescribed heirs from discretionary bequests, often discussing a limit of one-third for non-heir gifts and the question of consent for certain exceptions. This is not an unconditional permission to rewrite prescribed heir shares.','Record charitable intentions as topics for a specialist rather than specifying percentages that the site cannot verify.'],source:['Sahih al-Bukhari 2742 – One-third bequest discussion','https://sunnah.com/bukhari:2742']},
 {id:'will-england',title:'Signing a will in England and Wales',body:['GOV.UK explains that a valid will generally needs to be made voluntarily by an eligible adult of sound mind, in writing, and signed in the presence of two adult witnesses who also sign in the testator’s presence. Witness beneficiaries and their spouses are subject to restrictions.','Separate rules exist in Scotland and Northern Ireland. If you have assets outside the UK, different national laws or tax issues may apply; get appropriate cross-border advice.'],source:['GOV.UK – Make sure your will is legal','https://www.gov.uk/make-will/make-sure-your-will-is-legal']},
 {id:'will-checklist',title:'Preparation checklist for a solicitor',body:['Make a non-sensitive inventory of types of assets and liabilities; list potential heirs and relevant family relationships; consider executors and guardians; and identify where legal records are held. Do not paste card numbers, passwords or authentication secrets into a general-purpose worksheet.','A solicitor can help distinguish assets passing under the will from pensions, jointly held property, nominated benefits and trusts. An Islamic specialist can advise how those arrangements interact with your religious wishes.'],points:['Location of property and other significant assets','Outstanding liabilities and funeral arrangements','Surviving relatives and possible heirs','Executor, guardianship and professional contacts','Cross-border assets or prior wills','Charitable intentions and a review of tax/legal effects']},
 {id:'will-example',title:'Worked example: a family with a spouse and children',body:['A person has a spouse, dependent children, a home, savings and a pension. It may be unclear what legally forms part of their estate and which relatives qualify as heirs.','The worksheet captures the questions and documents to discuss, but it intentionally produces no percentages or inheritance verdict.'],example:'Prepare categories of assets and debts, list family relationships, identify executors and bring questions to both a solicitor and a qualified inheritance scholar.'}
 ],
 questions:[['Is the downloaded TXT file a will?','No. It is preparation notes only and has not been executed or witnessed.'],['Does this work in Scotland or Northern Ireland?','It can organise questions, but legal formalities differ. Choose legal advice for the correct jurisdiction.'],['Will Sunnah.tools retain my entries?','The form keeps them in the open page only unless you download a copy. Avoid entering sensitive credentials.']]
 },
 'aqiqah-planner':{
 intro:'Aqiqah planning brings together the seventh-day narration, alternative date-counting conventions and the practical questions families face.',
 sections:[
 {id:'aqiqah-meaning',title:'What is Aqiqah?',body:['Aqiqah is a sacrifice associated with welcoming a newborn. It is distinct from Eid al-Adha sacrifice and is discussed in reports about a newborn’s seventh day.','Scholarly discussions differ about its legal classification, how to handle a missed seventh day and which practices accompany it.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 2838 – Seventh day','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2838']},
 {id:'aqiqah-seventh',title:'How is the seventh day counted?',body:['A simple civil-day convention counts the Gregorian date of birth as day one, producing day seven six days later. Other approaches may exclude the birth day, and Islamic dates begin at sunset.','The calculator shows both date-counting illustrations so users can check the convention taught by their scholar; it does not determine a particular family’s religious date automatically.'],example:'Birth on Friday 30 October: counting birth day as day one gives Thursday 5 November; beginning the count the next day produces Friday 6 November.'},
 {id:'aqiqah-animals',title:'Number of animals and scholarly details',body:['Reports in Jami at-Tirmidhi discuss two similar sheep for a boy and one for a girl. Rules on species, quality, ability, timing and substitutions require qualified guidance; users should not assume that a calculator can certify a provider or the suitability of an animal.','Use the optional note fields to plan questions for a reputable provider instead of treating these numbers as a price quotation.'],source:['Jami at-Tirmidhi 1513 – Two and one','https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:1513']},
 {id:'aqiqah-naming',title:'Naming, hair and feeding people',body:['The seventh-day report also refers to naming and shaving the child’s head, while scholars discuss related details, appropriate methods and circumstances. Be guided by safety and knowledgeable advice, particularly for infants.','Families may distribute meat or provide food in different ways. Arrange slaughter and food handling with safe, lawful, humane practices and the applicable regulations.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 2838 – Naming and shaving','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2838']},
 {id:'aqiqah-later',title:'What if the seventh day is missed?',body:['Some scholars discuss the 14th, 21st or later opportunities; there are differences about the supporting evidence and how those dates should be counted. The page labels them as later references rather than fixed universal deadlines.','No family should assume the religious acceptability of a plan solely from a calendar conversion.']},
 {id:'aqiqah-steps',title:'Practical arrangement checklist',body:['Confirm your understanding of the relevant ruling, decide who will carry out the sacrifice, verify reputable service provision, consider animal welfare and safe food distribution, and record contact arrangements privately.','Keep the optional checklist about planning and evidence. Do not enter personal baby health details or payment credentials into a general-purpose web form.'],points:['Confirm school-specific timing with a scholar','Check animal/provider suitability and local rules','Choose a safe way to share food or donate','Review naming customs and infant safety','Keep receipt and contact details somewhere secure']}
 ],
 questions:[['Must Aqiqah happen exactly on the seventh day?','The seventh day is discussed in a hadith, but scholarly guidance differs on later performance and counting.'],['Is the number of animals identical for every family?','Reports commonly distinguish two for a boy and one for a girl, while ability and circumstances warrant qualified advice.'],['Does the website arrange a slaughter?','No. It only helps you plan and review dates.']]
 },
 'sunnah-fasting-planner':{
 intro:'A voluntary-fasting reference that distinguishes weekly habits, lunar-date practices, special days and days excluded from ordinary voluntary fasts.',
 sections:[
 {id:'fast-weekly',title:'Mondays and Thursdays',body:['There are reports about the Prophet ﷺ fasting on Mondays and Thursdays. The planner lists these Gregorian weekdays as potential voluntary fasts and labels overlaps with lunar-date recommendations.','Whether a particular person should fast depends on health, obligations, ability and individual fiqh considerations.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 2436 – Monday and Thursday','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2436']},
 {id:'fast-white',title:'White Days: 13, 14 and 15 Hijri',body:['Ayyam al-Bid are commonly associated with the 13th, 14th and 15th of each Islamic month. Our calculator converts dates using the Umm al-Qura scheme and allows an illustrative one-day adjustment, but it cannot know your local authority’s moon-sighting decision.','The 13th of Dhul Hijjah falls in the days of Tashriq and is not exported as an ordinary voluntary fast. Ramadan days are obligatory for those to whom fasting applies, not separate voluntary White Days.'],source:['Sunan Abi Dawud 2449 – White Days','https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2449']},
 {id:'fast-ashura',title:'Ashura and the ninth of Muharram',body:['Ashura falls on 10 Muharram, with a report in Sahih Muslim that the Prophet ﷺ intended to also fast the ninth in a following year. The planner identifies these as date references; it does not claim a special fixed hour.','Some scholars discuss adding a day before or after Ashura. Confirm your preferred ruling and the local Islamic date.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 1134a – Ninth of Muharram','https://sunnah.com/muslim:1134a']},
 {id:'fast-arafah',title:'The day of Arafah',body:['The ninth of Dhul Hijjah is the day of Arafah. Voluntary fasting on that day is generally discussed for people who are not performing Hajj; pilgrims have different practical and scholarly considerations.','The calendar labels the day “Arafah (for non-pilgrims)” rather than recommending it to everyone.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 1162b – Fasting Arafah','https://sunnah.com/muslim:1162b']},
 {id:'fast-shawwal',title:'Six fasts of Shawwal are flexible dates',body:['Sahih Muslim 1164a discusses six days of fasting in Shawwal after Ramadan. They are not six universal fixed dates on the calendar. The app therefore provides guidance on arranging them but does not automatically mark every Shawwal date as a required fast.','Whether missed Ramadan fasts must be made up before the six days, and sequencing advice, differ among scholars and depend on circumstances.'],source:['Sahih Muslim 1164a – Six days of Shawwal','https://sunnah.com/muslim:1164a']},
 {id:'fast-exclusions',title:'What does the calendar exclude?',body:['The two Eid days are explicitly prohibited fasting days in authentic hadith. The days of Tashriq (11–13 Dhul Hijjah) generally cannot be used for ordinary voluntary fasts; limited Hajj-related exceptions are discussed in fiqh.','Ramadan is never labelled as optional in this planner. You can show excluded dates in the table to see why they are not in calendar exports.'],source:['Sahih al-Bukhari 1990 – Two Eids','https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1990']},
 {id:'fast-example',title:'Worked example and calendar export',body:['Suppose a Monday is also the 13th of a Hijri month. Both categories can appear on the same date; downloading the calendar creates one event, not two duplicate fasting obligations.','Use the category filters to focus on weekly dates, White Days or special dates, then export only eligible dates. Recheck with local moon sighting before acting.'],example:'A Monday White Day is one Gregorian date with two labels. If the date falls in Ramadan or on a prohibited day, the export still excludes it.'}
 ],
 questions:[['Does it include the six days of Shawwal automatically?','No. Those six dates can be chosen flexibly, so the guide explains them rather than presenting arbitrary fixed Shawwal dates.'],['Why do some dates disappear from the export?','Ramadan, Eid and ordinary voluntary fasting during Tashriq are excluded. User-selected category filters may also reduce the export.'],['Can I import the calendar as guaranteed local dates?','No. Every Hijri conversion is an estimate that must be checked against local announcements.']]
 }
};
const {slug}=Astro.props;
const guide=data[String(slug??'')];
---
{guide&&<section class="seven-reference" id="in-depth-reference" aria-labelledby="seven-reference-heading">
 <div class="seven-reference-header"><p class="seven-reference-eyebrow">Detailed reference and examples</p><h2 id="seven-reference-heading">A complete guide</h2><p>{guide.intro}</p></div>
 <nav class="seven-guide-nav" aria-label="Sections in the detailed guide">{guide.sections.map(({id,title},i)=><a href={`#${id}`}>{i+1}. {title}</a>)}<a href="#seven-reference-questions">More questions</a></nav>
 <div class="seven-reference-sections">
 {guide.sections.map(({id,title,body,example,points,source},i)=><details class="seven-reference-item" id={id} open={i===0}>
  <summary><span class="seven-section-no">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>{title}</strong><span class="seven-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
  <div class="seven-reference-content">{body.map(paragraph=><p>{paragraph}</p>)}
   {points&&<ul>{points.map(point=><li>{point}</li>)}</ul>}
   {example&&<p class="seven-example"><strong>Worked example:</strong> {example}</p>}
   {source&&<p class="seven-source"><a href={source[1]} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{source[0]} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>}
  </div>
 </details>)}
 </div>
 <section id="seven-reference-questions" class="seven-reference-faq"><h3>Further questions</h3>
 {guide.questions.map(([question,answer])=><details><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</section>
 <p class="seven-reference-footer">Educational guidance only. Where dates, local rules, clinical decisions or legal outcomes matter, verify them with a qualified professional or religious authority. No live moon-sighting or medical decisions are provided.</p>
</section>}
<style>
.seven-reference{display:grid;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--brand-line);padding-top:27px;margin:24px 0 32px}
.seven-reference-eyebrow{font:700 11px/1.5 var(--font-body);color:var(--brand-accent);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;margin:0 0 4px}
.seven-reference-header h2{font:600 clamp(26px,3vw,33px)/1.2 var(--font-display);margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--brand-ink)}
.seven-reference-header>p:last-child{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;max-width:76ch;margin:0;color:var(--brand-copy)}
.seven-guide-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px}
.seven-guide-nav a{text-decoration:none;font:600 11px/1.5 var(--font-body);border:1px solid var(--brand-line);background:var(--brand-soft);color:var(--brand-ink);border-radius:25px;padding:7px 12px}
.seven-guide-nav a:hover{border-color:var(--brand-accent);text-decoration:underline}
.seven-reference-sections{display:grid;gap:11px}
.seven-reference-item{border:1px solid var(--brand-line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--brand-card);scroll-margin-top:90px;overflow:hidden}
.seven-reference-item summary{list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;cursor:pointer;padding:18px;color:var(--brand-ink)}
.seven-reference-item summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.seven-reference-item summary strong{font:650 15px/1.4 var(--font-body);flex:1}
.seven-section-no{font:700 11px/1.2 var(--font-body);color:var(--brand-accent);min-width:25px}
.seven-expand-icon{font-size:21px;font-weight:400;transition:transform .2s}
.seven-reference-item[open] .seven-expand-icon{transform:rotate(45deg)}
.seven-reference-content{padding:2px 20px 21px 56px;display:grid;gap:12px}
